This study introduces a monotone cubic spline interpolation formula for $y$ values that are linked to $x$ values with high rates of change. The derived expression for interpolating any given function follows the mathematical form:

\begin{equation}
y_i(y_{i+1}-y_i)+(h/3)(y_{i+1}+y_i)(y_{i+1}-y_i)y_i+h^3(y_{i+1}^2y_i-y_i^3)/(6h),
\end{equation}

where the expression for the interpolated value $y_i$ depends on the linked points $y_{i+1}$ and $y_i$, along with the step size $h$. This formula maintains monotonicity and differentiability, and its local truncation error is $h^3(y_{i+1}^2y_i-y_i^3)/(3h)$. A comparison of the proposed method with the existing monotonic cubic interpolation technique reveals that the new formula offers improved approximation, faster computation, and greater precision.
